      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "The holmium complex has a highly axial site magnetic structure, but large tunnel splittings of the ground doublet for this non-Kramers ion. Slow relaxation is observed, with a broadened χ''(T) peak and incomplete Cole–Cole semicircles, and a thermal barrier much lower than that of the dysprosium analogue.",
        "measurements": [
